  "id": "runtime-limits-ceilings",
  "description": "Plan v7 section 8.3 runtime-limits clause: every limit set to its hard ceiling (MAXIMUM_NUMBER_PRECISION 4096, MAXIMUM_ABSOLUTE_NUMBER_SCALE 4096, MAXIMUM_VISIBLE_DECIMAL_PLACES 4096, MAXIMUM_COMPACT_EXPONENT 4096, MAXIMUM_EXPRESSION_CHARACTERS 4096, MAXIMUM_EXPRESSION_TOKENS 512, MAXIMUM_EXPRESSION_NESTING_DEPTH 64, MAXIMUM_GENERATED_PLACEHOLDER_DEPTH 64, MAXIMUM_INTERPOLATED_OUTPUT_CHARACTERS 1048576, MAXIMUM_GENERATED_EXPANSION_CHARACTERS 8388608), all read from TranslationRuntimeLimits.java lines 80-101. Builder.build's validateCeiling rejects anything above a ceiling, so the fixture constructing at all pins the ceilings from below. The cases then show two values that fail under the defaults succeeding here — pinning that the configured limit, not a hardcoded default, governs at runtime — and one that still fails, pinning that PluralOperands.Builder's own bound is not reached by the instance configuration.",
